@startuml truth_table_class
title plogic - TruthTable

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class Interpreter

class TruthTable {
  -variables: List<str>
  -rows: List<Row>
  -label: str
  -simplified: str?
  --
  +with_display(label: str, simplified: str?): TruthTable
  +classify(): Classification
}

class Row {
  -values: List<bool>
  -result: bool
}

enum Classification {
  Tautology
  Contradiction
  Contingency
}

class InfixPrinter

class Orchestrator

interface UI

note bottom of TruthTable
  One column per distinct variable of the evaluated
  expression (the original by default, the simplified one
  with --tabla-simplificada), in order of first
  appearance; one row per assignment (2^n), in binary
  counting order with the last variable varying fastest.

  The result column is labelled with the evaluated
  expression in normalized form: the operand order the
  user wrote for the original, canonical order for the
  simplified formula. simplified is present only when the
  Simplifier ran and uses canonical order; with
  --tabla-simplificada it repeats the label. Both texts
  are produced by InfixPrinter. with_display returns a new
  table; there are no setters.
end note

note bottom of Classification
  Tautology: the result column is all V.
  Contradiction: the result column is all F.
  Contingency: anything else.
  Classification reads the column, not the simplified
  formula, so it stays exact. It is always shown.
end note

Interpreter ..> TruthTable : <<create>>
TruthTable --> Row : rows
TruthTable --> Classification : classify
Orchestrator ..> TruthTable : with_display
Orchestrator ..> InfixPrinter : <<use>>
UI ..> TruthTable : <<use>>

@enduml
